# A generic cannot be a union member: at [int] and [str] the union would
# have two list members, and `list l` would bind the wrong one. This
# program checked before the rule was enforced in signatures, and then
# added 1 to "x".
def g (a b -- a | b) swap drop end
[1] ["x"] g match list l : @l 0 nth 1 + wl, _ : end
